## Why This Is Asked
Tests low-level arithmetic with 128-bit values, ensuring correct carry propagation and branchless coding. It mirrors real-world bit-twiddling tasks in crypto, compression, or hash pipelines where performance and correctness matter.

## Key Concepts

- Carry propagation across 64-bit boundaries
- 128-bit arithmetic using hi/lo
- Branchless implementation using comparisons as carry indicators

## Code Example

```c
uint128 add128(uint128 a, uint128 b, unsigned *carryOut) {
  uint64_t lo = a.lo + b.lo;
  unsigned c0 = lo < a.lo;
  uint64_t hi = a.hi + b.hi + c0;
  unsigned c1 = hi < a.hi;
  *carryOut = c1;
  return (uint128){.hi = hi, .lo = lo};
}
```

